Plane walls, composite layers and energy closure (@th-plane: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD", #source "../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF", #source "../sources/Guarded-Hot-Plate-and-SRM-1450e-NIST.lingua#r_1PP28H0Y6N7RVY89W9HSQY18E4", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "Cylinders-spheres-and-changing-transfer-area.lingua#r_05G5H8FQXMWYDSEG2RF0RYD7A3") { r_4J8Z4W7NZGZ0N1MCE66CAGQHJF
**Read:** [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), complete steady plane/composite-wall sections; [Second Level Course in Heat Transfer — R. P. Vedula](../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF), one-dimensional steady conduction; [Guarded-hot-plate evidence — NIST SP 260-201](../sources/Guarded-Hot-Plate-and-SRM-1450e-NIST.lingua#r_1PP28H0Y6N7RVY89W9HSQY18E4), guarded one-dimensional measurement assumptions.

For steady one-dimensional conduction without internal generation, serial layers share the same heat rate and their temperature drops follow their resistances. Sum L/(kA) only when the geometry, area convention and constitutive assumptions support that expression. Add distinct contact and external transfer resistances where physically justified.

Derive interface temperatures and check that each layer's energy account closes. A large temperature drop identifies a large resistance under these conditions; it does not directly identify the material responsible without thickness and contact evidence. Parallel heat paths require a different network.

Work a complete multilayer example, then change one contact resistance and an external temperature. Compare an analytical resistance calculation with the steady limit of [An inspectable conservative transient layered slab](../computation/An-inspectable-conservative-transient-layered-slab.lingua#r_6B5B7E7C3Z1APY0RYAC09P12ET). The independently derived agreement verifies the restricted numerical model; measurements still determine whether it describes the physical assembly.

**Continue:** [Cylinders, spheres and changing transfer area](Cylinders-spheres-and-changing-transfer-area.lingua#r_05G5H8FQXMWYDSEG2RF0RYD7A3).

